   "source": [
    "### Interpreting the final model\n",
    "\n",
    "Because both the target and numerical predictors are log-transformed, numerical coefficients are interpreted approximately as elasticities: a 1% increase in a numerical predictor is associated with approximately a coefficient-percent change in expected units sold, holding other predictors constant, particularly for small percentage changes.\n",
    "\n",
    "Categorical coefficients compare the corresponding category with its reference category on the modeled log-sales scale.\n",
    "\n",
    "These coefficients represent model-based associations, not proof of causal effects."
   ]
